{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1423168-any-reason-for-a-sidereal-not-to-use-the-ride-prayer-strip-charm","id":1423168,"title":"Any reason for a Sidereal not to use the Ride Prayer strip charm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-11T20:01:53-08:00","id":1423168,"title":"Any reason for a Sidereal not to use the Ride Prayer strip charm","content":"If you use it on a connection with the willpower Sacrifice a reason not to if you like the connection in question enough?<br /> <br /> A Permanent Willpower Dot is a terrible Sacrifice<br /> <br /> <br /> but I See it as so worth it if you want to grant a friend immortality and power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T02:14:11-08:00","id":1423224,"title":"","content":"Which edition are we talking about here?<br /> <br /> I assume it's 2E (I don't recall how the 1E power works).<br /> <br /> You're taking a trusted mortal friend, one of your limited contacts in the world, and turning them into a Dragon for some kind of urgent emergency -- do you really want to go into that emergency 1 WP down? And consider the training times for buying that dot of WP back up. And the OOC cost of just taking an existing Lesser Elemental Dragon as an ally. And that mortal shopkeeper in Nexus is gone: it's one more god in heaven, but you've got no shortage of friendly gods in heaven... and you've purchased it with one of your precious mortal friends.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, I'd spend the willpower if I had it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T09:31:00-08:00","id":1423300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1423168-any-reason-for-a-sidereal-not-to-use-the-ride-prayer-strip-charm?p=1423224#post1423224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it's 2E (I don't recall how the 1E power works).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the same, but you didn't get the option of burning off a dot of Willpower to keep the Acquaintance/Familiar's mind intact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T07:33:44-08:00","id":1423550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1423168-any-reason-for-a-sidereal-not-to-use-the-ride-prayer-strip-charm?p=1423300#post1423300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly the same, but you didn't get the option of burning off a dot of Willpower to keep the Acquaintance/Familiar's mind intact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the op seems to regard the charm as a method of granting apotheosis (which in 2e it absolutely has the potential to be), this one change is a tremendous deal, and drastically reshapes the use and spirit of the charm: permanently and completely ruining a trusted contact because you need that dragon *now* (tbh completely in the themes of 1e Sidereals), vs a meaningful sacrifice that permanently empowers an ally (though I guess if you were a bad person you could just let them be a gibbering husk after you were done).<br /> <br /> The possibility of ameliorating the terrible human cost of the charm drastically alters its focus, and in 1e, a topic like this would be &quot;why *would* you use this charm (you monster)?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T08:40:59-08:00","id":1423565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1423168-any-reason-for-a-sidereal-not-to-use-the-ride-prayer-strip-charm?p=1423550#post1423550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that the op seems to regard the charm as a method of granting apotheosis (which in 2e it absolutely has the potential to be), this one change is a tremendous deal, and drastically reshapes the use and spirit of the charm: permanently and completely ruining a trusted contact because you need that dragon *now* (tbh completely in the themes of 1e Sidereals), vs a meaningful sacrifice that permanently empowers an ally (though I guess if you were a bad person you could just let them be a gibbering husk after you were done).<br /> <br /> The possibility of ameliorating the terrible human cost of the charm drastically alters its focus, and in 1e, a topic like this would be &quot;why *would* you use this charm (you monster)?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very good point indeed about how the addition of the permanent WP sacrifice option utterly altered the tenor of the charm between editions. That creates an interesting conundrum over what direction to take it into 3rd edition, how to balance or not views and expectations created by the different versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-13-2020, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T23:54:45-08:00","id":1423686,"title":"","content":"Helping them set themselves up would be an adventure i n itself I think. Helping them find employment somewhere in Yu-shan<br /> <br /> Gain a Salary<br /> <br /> or maybe just a manse.<br /> <br /> Best to invite them as guests into your Celestial manse first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T20:57:27-08:00","id":1501001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1423168-any-reason-for-a-sidereal-not-to-use-the-ride-prayer-strip-charm?p=1423686#post1423686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Helping them set themselves up would be an adventure i n itself I think. Helping them find employment somewhere in Yu-shan<br /> <br /> Gain a Salary<br /> <br /> or maybe just a manse.<br /> <br /> Best to invite them as guests into your Celestial manse first?</div> </div> </div> </div>OR it could stay in Creation and make itself into a very big fish in a smaller and more familiar pond instead.<br /> <br /> Just a matter of learning a charm to return to human form or one close enough if desirous of immersing oneself back into mortal society, its old shopkeeper job even if more confortable doing so, with maybe some funny excuse/tale if looking somehow different now due to some supernatural tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-22-2023, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}